// FnArg.fol — package source file
// Spec: language-ref.md > Functions Taking and Returning Functions >
//       Syntax 2 — Named type alias
//
// A function TYPE named through co.lang.type. This is the argument-position
// half of the spec's `someFArg` / `someFRet` pair:
//
//     someFunction(r FnArg)->(FnRet) = {}
//
// It binds a type expression, so the declaration ends with a semicolon.
//
// Three spellings that are easy to confuse:
//
//     FnArg    co.lang.type     = (co.lang.int, co.lang.int)->(co.lang.int);
//     BinaryOp co.lang.delegate = (co.lang.int, co.lang.int)->(co.lang.int);
//     Handler  co.lang.function = (a co.lang.int)->(co.lang.int) = { ... }
//
// The first two are TYPES — a type alias and a named call shape. The third is
// a concrete function VALUE.

_ co.lang.type = (co.lang.int, co.lang.int)->(co.lang.int);
